The attached image (Fig. 5) illustrates how Nano-11 facilitates antigen transport to draining lymph nodes. Flow cytometry plots (A) show the detection and phenotyping of ovalbumin (OVA) positive cells, indicating that Nano-11 (OVA+N11) leads to a higher mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA compared to OVA alone or OVA with aluminum hydroxide (OVA+AH) on both Day 1 and Day 2 (B). Furthermore, Nano-11 significantly increases the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among OVA-positive cells in the draining lymph nodes (C), demonstrating its superior efficiency in delivering antigens to highly immunopotentiating MigDCs on a per-cell basis.